1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,500
PHANTOM GRID demonstrates hardware-level cyber defense against rogue automotive nodes.

2
00:00:03,500 --> 00:00:07,500
When unauthorized CAN ID 0x666 or firmware tampering is detected, an E-Fuse trip is triggered.

3
00:00:07,500 --> 00:00:12,000
In 1.8 microseconds, 100A peak cutoff current blows the circuit, permanently isolating transceiver pins.

4
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:16,000
The node signature is computed and indelibly stamped into an immutable SHA-256 blacklist audit log.

5
00:00:16,000 --> 00:00:20,000
Exposed via vehicle MCP tools for autonomous AI Agent monitoring and fleet-wide Nostr mesh warning.
